  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="3">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Northleoda">Norðleoda</ref> 3</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="3" corresp="#wit-h">Bisceopes 7 ealdermannes VIII þusend þrymsa.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="3" corresp="#wit-q">Episcopi et aldermanni octo milia þrimsa.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="3" corresp="#wit-d">Biscopes 7 ealdormannes VIII þusend ðrymsa.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock" corresp="#wit-d">That of a bishop and an ealdorman 8,000 <hi rend="italic">thrymsas</hi>.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin" corresp="#wit-h">Bishops and ealdormen, eight thousand <hi rend="italic">thrymsas</hi>.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">eines Bischofs und Ealdorman 8000 Tremissen [100 Pfund],</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">of a bishop and an ealdorman 8,000 thrymsas [100 pounds],</ab>
        <note type="editorial">and ‘ðrymsa’ corrected to H's ‘þrymsa’. Liebermann compares the Instituta Cnuti III 57: ‘Episcopus et comes habent … leges equales’.</note>
      </div>
    </body>
